==English==
{{wp|dab=alveolus}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|alveolus||a small hollow or cavity}}, diminutive of {{m|la|alveus||a hollow, cavity}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˌal.viˈəʊ.ləs/|/alˈviː.əl.əs/}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ælˈvi.əl.əs/}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːələs}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|alveoli}}

# A [[small]] [[cavity]] or [[pit]].
## {{lb|en|anatomy}} Any of the many tiny [[air sac]]s in the [[lung]]s in which the [[bronchiole]]s [[terminate]] and where [[oxygen]] and [[carbon dioxide]] are rapidly {{w|gas exchange|exchanged}} with the [[pulmonary]] [[capillary|capillaries]].
##: {{syn|en|pulmonary alveolus}}
## {{lb|en|anatomy|dentistry}} The [[bony]] [[socket]] in which the [[root]] of a [[tooth]] [[reside]]s.
##: {{syn|en|dental alveolus|tooth socket}}
## {{lb|en|anatomy}} An [[acinus]] {{gl|[[saclike]] [[cavity]]}} in a [[gland]].
## {{lb|en|entomology}} The [[socket]] of a [[macrotrichium]] {{gl|[[seta]]}}.

